<%#
  "Load more" control for the board activity feed.

  The wrapper renders even when there's nothing more to load: it's the
  turbo_stream replace target, and replacing a missing target is silently
  dropped — so an always-present wrapper is what lets the last page empty the
  control out instead of leaving a dead button behind.

  data-turbo-stream makes this GET link ask for a turbo-stream response, so the
  next page APPENDS to the feed rather than navigating or replacing it. Turbo
  intercepts links carrying that attribute (FormLinkClickObserver) and reissues
  them as a stream request — no custom JS needed.

  Not a turbo-frame: a link inside a frame gets frame-navigated, which would
  swap the control's own markup in place of the rows. A plain id + explicit
  replace keeps the two effects separate.

  locals: board (Board), has_more (Boolean), next_page (Integer)
%>
<div id="activity_load_more_frame" class="mt-4 text-center">
  <% if has_more %>
    <%= link_to activity_board_path(board, page: next_page),
        id: "activity_load_more",
        data: { turbo_stream: true },
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink-700 bg-white border border-line rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:bg-surface-50 hover:border-ink-300 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-700 focus-visible:ring-offset-1" do %>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down text-xs text-ink-500" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      Load more
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
